[Applause]  my name is dr david michael smith and  i'm a member of the houston united front  against fascism  [Music]  the anti-fascist movement is pretty  diverse a lot of attention has been paid  to some of the younger folks that dress  in black and you know often are  anarchists or anarcho-socialists houston  united front against fascism  has a little bit different approach  some of us have come from communist and  socialist backgrounds others are just  genuinely progressive folks on the left  but we do like working with everybody  including the so-called antifa black  bloc in fighting against fascism and  trumpsterism our organization was formed  to oppose  the trump movement neo-nazis other  fascists that have taken to the streets  of greater houston over the last several  years so we sponsor militant but  non-violent protest we educate people  about the threat posed by the far right  and we're glad to have played a role in  the defeat of trump nationally we're  contributing here in houston but also  nationally to the spike in homicides and  that's what i would call a growing  legitimacy of our police agencies in the  united states in the wake of the murder  of george floyd you've had massive  massive protests more than 15 million  people protest in the summer of 2020 and  even though they did not produce a lot  of police reforms it has had an effect  in the communities across this country a  lot of young people who might be  inclined to commit potentially violent  crimes are now asking well if the cops  don't have to obey the law why should i  and this is a huge huge problem  everybody agrees that violent crime is a  problem there's no disagreement about  that but our elected officials and  politicians need to hear from the  community that not all of us want more  cops or harsher policing we need to get  at the root causes of the problem we  need to tackle poverty racism economic  inequality and all the rest so look i'm  not an anarchist i'm a communist i  definitely believe in having law  enforcement in whatever kind of society  you want but you've got to have law  enforcement that's answerable and  accountable to the communities we need  democratic community control of the  police in our country our country not  just houston has always had a huge  homicide problem social scientists all  know that we have the most  violent kind of society the highest  homicide rate of any of the advanced  capitalist countries and it has gotten  worse in the last two years  if you look at statistics from the  centers for disease control a department  of justice in washington  we know that the hike and uh or spike in  homicides has occurred in part because  of covet you know kobe's had a lot of  really bad effects on people  psychologically financially and so forth  so that's part of it you know another  part in houston that's peculiar to  houston is that we have a terribly  backlash backlogged court problem you  know basically we had hurricane harvey  in 2017 and then covet over the last  couple years and that combination has  led to check this out about 100 000  cases that have not been heard yet and  some of which involve people who are  still out on the street and able to  commit crimes again so i think that when  you look at you know covet and houston  the backlog of court cases and this  legitimation crisis for the police i  think those explain the most recent  spikes

